The IP-PAD UK data come from four online surveys of young people in the United Kingdom, carried out between 2024 and 2026. Two fieldwork providers each ran two waves. Gallup International interviewed young people who are members of its online panels themselves, while Survation reached younger adolescents through the panel accounts of their parents. We combined the four surveys into one data file with one row per interview, which holds 4,968 interviews with 4,841 young people. Apart from two questions about the future that only Survation asked, the file includes only questions that were asked in at least two of the surveys, so that answers can be compared between them.

